1
00:01:04,428 --> 00:01:06,961
Alright, let's try it again.

2
00:01:13,583 --> 00:01:16,353
We'll keep it. One more take.

3
00:01:21,996 --> 00:01:24,477
Just one more time.

4
00:01:30,392 --> 00:01:32,992
We'll keep this. One more take.

5
00:01:34,539 --> 00:01:36,412
We'll just keep this one too.

6
00:01:37,318 --> 00:01:38,949
Gyu Hui.

7
00:01:38,949 --> 00:01:40,858
Gyu Hui.

8
00:01:40,858 --> 00:01:42,418
Gyu Hui.

9
00:01:43,318 --> 00:01:45,473
I can't do this.

10
00:01:45,473 --> 00:01:47,426
Why?

11
00:01:47,426 --> 00:01:48,912
Hey...

12
00:01:54,749 --> 00:01:57,439
Of all days, Nara gets hospitalized today.

13
00:01:57,439 --> 00:02:00,629
And you had to make the song this hard.

14
00:02:00,629 --> 00:02:04,626
It's not like someone
who can play this just shows up.

15
00:02:04,626 --> 00:02:06,473
Maybe... Hee Jeong?

16
00:02:06,473 --> 00:02:07,736
Hee Jeong?

17
00:02:07,736 --> 00:02:09,936
You think I didn't try calling?

18
00:02:09,936 --> 00:02:11,193
She saw the score and said

19
00:02:11,193 --> 00:02:14,016
she'd need at least a week.

20
00:02:14,016 --> 00:02:15,913
I'm not blaming you.

21
00:02:15,913 --> 00:02:17,470
I'm just saying, take it easy.

22
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:20,133
Be a little more flexible.

23
00:02:20,729 --> 00:02:21,986
Huh?

24
00:02:21,986 --> 00:02:23,473
Yun Ju?

25
00:02:24,737 --> 00:02:26,530
Guess someone really did show up.

26
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:29,595
I heard you were back in Korea.

27
00:02:29,595 --> 00:02:31,875
Just didn't expect this.

28
00:03:12,148 --> 00:03:13,593
Hey, Do Hyun.

29
00:03:13,593 --> 00:03:15,986
Jun Kyung, have you eaten?

30
00:03:15,986 --> 00:03:18,440
I was waiting to eat with you.

31
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:19,893
Are you far from wrapping up?

32
00:03:19,893 --> 00:03:21,520
It might take a bit longer.

33
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:24,406
I think I'll eat with Jung Hoon later.

34
00:03:24,406 --> 00:03:26,040
Make sure you eat.

35
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:28,200
You must be hungry.

36
00:03:41,116 --> 00:03:43,273
Jin Ho.

37
00:03:43,273 --> 00:03:46,116
Have you seen Bom?

38
00:03:46,116 --> 00:03:48,356
I can't find her anywhere.

39
00:03:51,289 --> 00:03:52,943
Ja Yeong,

40
00:03:53,472 --> 00:03:55,233
are you okay?

41
00:03:57,200 --> 00:04:00,186
I must have dozed off for a second.

42
00:04:01,525 --> 00:04:03,585
I dreamed about Bom.

43
00:04:06,610 --> 00:04:09,703
It felt so real, I thought it was happening.

44
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,870
Gosh.

45
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:15,475
So it was just a dream.

46
00:04:17,009 --> 00:04:18,921
That must have scared you.

47
00:04:18,921 --> 00:04:20,663
Yeah.

48
00:04:20,663 --> 00:04:22,543
I'm sorry.

49
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:28,737
You just need to have 5 million ready.

50
00:04:29,295 --> 00:04:33,152
Lots of lecturers are eyeing
those general electives,

51
00:04:33,152 --> 00:04:35,050
and the complaints are endless.

52
00:04:35,050 --> 00:04:37,783
As long as you have that amount ready,
you should be fine.

53
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:44,770
Okay.

54
00:04:44,770 --> 00:04:46,482
Wrap it up and come quickly.

55
00:04:52,703 --> 00:04:54,643
The director liked it.

56
00:04:58,710 --> 00:05:00,070
Send your account info to Jung Hoon.

57
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:02,556
Isn't that a little too businesslike?

58
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:08,860
Thank you.

59
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:11,520
- Enjoy your meal.
- Wow, thanks.

60
00:05:13,199 --> 00:05:15,919
It's been ages since I've had hagfish.

61
00:05:18,979 --> 00:05:22,179
When I played earlier,
it brought back memories.

62
00:05:22,753 --> 00:05:25,764
Freshman year, on the street in Jongno,

63
00:05:25,764 --> 00:05:28,520
I played the piano, the song you made.

64
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:31,566
Remember how people crowded around?

65
00:05:38,345 --> 00:05:42,419
Do you know how much I liked you back then?

66
00:05:46,645 --> 00:05:49,485
Even those memories make you uncomfortable?

67
00:05:51,226 --> 00:05:54,172
I thought about the past too.

68
00:05:57,066 --> 00:05:58,595
Back then...

69
00:05:59,786 --> 00:06:02,385
I really liked you too.

70
00:06:06,676 --> 00:06:08,009
But...

71
00:06:09,809 --> 00:06:11,722
like you said,

72
00:06:11,722 --> 00:06:13,702
they're just memories.

73
00:06:25,309 --> 00:06:28,002
Sorry. I should get going.

74
00:06:28,496 --> 00:06:31,969
Jun Kyung is waiting. I shouldn't stay here.

75
00:06:40,613 --> 00:06:42,515
Then what about me?

76
00:06:44,499 --> 00:06:47,339
You're the one I need right now.

77
00:07:02,522 --> 00:07:05,272
We ended a long time ago.

78
00:07:08,559 --> 00:07:11,585
I'll do my best as Daniel's father,

79
00:07:13,887 --> 00:07:16,380
but that's all there is between us.

80
00:07:17,389 --> 00:07:19,019
Where are you going?

81
00:07:20,192 --> 00:07:21,773
Hey!

82
00:08:06,539 --> 00:08:08,745
I know.

83
00:08:10,239 --> 00:08:13,352
I know Jun Kyung is with Do Hyun now.

84
00:08:15,506 --> 00:08:18,059
But they've only been two years.

85
00:08:20,032 --> 00:08:22,778
We go way back.

86
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:27,333
And we have...

87
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:30,165
Daniel.

88
00:08:32,073 --> 00:08:34,886
I thought that made me stronger.

89
00:08:36,992 --> 00:08:39,538
There's no stronger or weaker.

90
00:08:47,358 --> 00:08:49,055
So...

91
00:08:49,055 --> 00:08:51,105
what are you going to do now?

92
00:08:52,050 --> 00:08:53,518
I don't know.

93
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:56,707
What do I do now?

94
00:09:03,981 --> 00:09:07,041
Joy and sadness

95
00:09:07,041 --> 00:09:10,340
always seem to come out of nowhere.

96
00:09:12,043 --> 00:09:16,100
Sadness especially.

97
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:22,223
There's a tribe in Africa

98
00:09:22,223 --> 00:09:25,746
that believes rain
is a sign of sorrow from God.

99
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:27,757
So when it rained,

100
00:09:27,757 --> 00:09:30,025
they stayed outside the village

101
00:09:30,025 --> 00:09:32,646
until the rain stopped,

102
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:36,264
until the sun came out

103
00:09:36,264 --> 00:09:38,635
and the ground dried.

104
00:09:39,944 --> 00:09:41,948
In Seoul right now,

105
00:09:41,948 --> 00:09:44,608
rain is falling without warning.

106
00:09:46,514 --> 00:09:48,771
Is it a sign of sorrow

107
00:09:48,771 --> 00:09:51,017
God is sending us?

108
00:09:52,380 --> 00:09:54,104
Everyone,

109
00:09:54,104 --> 00:09:56,610
did you bring an umbrella?

110
00:10:01,686 --> 00:10:04,147
I also used to touch Bom like this,

111
00:10:04,147 --> 00:10:06,760
and she'd stay so still.

112
00:10:07,666 --> 00:10:11,306
I still remember how soft
the back of her head felt.

113
00:10:13,752 --> 00:10:15,900
The good memories

114
00:10:16,387 --> 00:10:18,613
are what make it harder.

115
00:10:20,693 --> 00:10:22,759
If I'd known it would be like this,

116
00:10:22,759 --> 00:10:25,785
I wouldn't have tried so hard.

117
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:32,486
That memory wipe package,

118
00:10:32,486 --> 00:10:34,612
do you think it still exists?

119
00:10:37,130 --> 00:10:39,880
You remember those travelers we saw in Jeju,

120
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:41,643
when we were eating?

121
00:10:42,936 --> 00:10:44,692
Jin Ho.

122
00:10:46,596 --> 00:10:48,763
Don't you hear that?

123
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:54,233
The rain?

124
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:25,613
Jun Kyung, where did you go?

125
00:11:25,613 --> 00:11:27,560
It's pouring out there.

126
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:30,119
You should've taken an umbrella.

127
00:11:31,766 --> 00:11:34,359
Umbrellas always seem close,

128
00:11:34,879 --> 00:11:37,419
but never there when you need them.

129
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,966
I lied to you.

130
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:55,933
Earlier,

131
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,986
when we were on the phone,

132
00:12:01,373 --> 00:12:03,299
I was with Yun Ju.

133
00:12:07,279 --> 00:12:10,012
I thought it might make you uncomfortable,

134
00:12:12,636 --> 00:12:14,542
so I didn't say anything.

135
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:19,796
I thought lying would be better.

136
00:12:28,104 --> 00:12:29,404
I'm sorry.

137
00:12:32,286 --> 00:12:34,751
I went by your studio earlier.

138
00:12:42,610 --> 00:12:45,122
Thank you for being honest with me.

139
00:13:13,139 --> 00:13:15,453
I've thought about it a lot.

140
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:18,593
And I just...

141
00:13:19,166 --> 00:13:21,546
I wish now were the right time.

142
00:13:30,923 --> 00:13:33,170
When you need me,

143
00:13:34,643 --> 00:13:36,663
and when you don't,

144
00:13:38,642 --> 00:13:40,129
I'll always

145
00:13:41,169 --> 00:13:43,642
be right by your side.

146
00:13:58,141 --> 00:13:59,614
Jun Kyung.

147
00:14:01,788 --> 00:14:04,468
Will you marry me?

148
00:14:35,901 --> 00:14:38,460
- Hello, Dad.
- Hello.

149
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:39,680
Are you busy right now?

150
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:41,980
I'm okay. What's going on?

151
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:44,333
It's nothing serious.

152
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,780
It's about Ja Yeong.

153
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:50,922
She seemed better after coming here,

154
00:14:50,922 --> 00:14:52,735
but she's not sleeping well,

155
00:14:52,735 --> 00:14:55,026
she seems more on edge lately,

156
00:14:55,026 --> 00:14:57,465
and kind of down too.

157
00:14:58,059 --> 00:15:00,599
I heard there's something
called pet loss syndrome.

158
00:15:00,599 --> 00:15:03,300
Maybe that's what she's going through.

159
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:04,976
Pet loss syndrome?

160
00:15:04,976 --> 00:15:06,100
Yeah.

161
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:10,766
A lot of people get counseling
after losing a pet.

162
00:15:12,493 --> 00:15:15,492
She lost family, after all.

163
00:15:19,450 --> 00:15:20,770
Oh, right.

164
00:15:20,770 --> 00:15:22,970
Why don't you come visit
with Do Hyun and Jun Seo?

165
00:15:22,970 --> 00:15:24,850
It's been a while since I've seen you.

166
00:15:24,850 --> 00:15:27,316
I miss Daniel too.

167
00:15:27,316 --> 00:15:29,550
We'll come, Dad.

168
00:15:29,550 --> 00:15:31,290
Sorry I haven't checked in more.

169
00:15:31,290 --> 00:15:33,210
I know you're busy. Thanks.

170
00:15:33,210 --> 00:15:34,417
Okay.

171
00:15:34,417 --> 00:15:36,250
By the way...

172
00:15:37,343 --> 00:15:39,523
You're doing alright, right?

173
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:45,280
I'm fine.

174
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:47,400
Okay. See you soon.

175
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:49,533
Okay.

176
00:16:00,153 --> 00:16:01,847
Ja Yeong.

177
00:16:02,652 --> 00:16:04,765
What are you staring at like that?

178
00:16:13,073 --> 00:16:14,966
The five-day market should be open today.

179
00:16:14,966 --> 00:16:16,880
Want to go check it out?

180
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:18,648
We can grab a few things,

181
00:16:18,648 --> 00:16:21,314
maybe have jajangmyeon for once.

182
00:16:21,314 --> 00:16:22,891
Jin Ho.

183
00:16:22,891 --> 00:16:24,557
Yeah?

184
00:16:24,557 --> 00:16:26,484
Coming here like this...

185
00:16:27,018 --> 00:16:29,544
Don't you think it was too rushed?

186
00:16:30,584 --> 00:16:33,770
Like we were running away.

187
00:16:39,619 --> 00:16:41,743
Jin Ho.

188
00:16:41,743 --> 00:16:43,496
Hey.

189
00:16:44,413 --> 00:16:46,120
Do you not like it here?

190
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,717
- What?
- Answer me.

191
00:16:47,717 --> 00:16:49,799
You don't like this place?

192
00:16:49,799 --> 00:16:52,440
- That's not...
- You said it yourself.

193
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:54,144
You wanted to live somewhere

194
00:16:54,144 --> 00:16:56,133
where the flowers bloom first,

195
00:16:56,133 --> 00:16:59,164
where the sun hits first,
where you step on fallen leaves first.

196
00:16:59,164 --> 00:17:01,420
You said it.

197
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:03,680
We weren't running away.

198
00:17:05,133 --> 00:17:08,306
I just felt a little trapped.

199
00:17:09,367 --> 00:17:11,683
I didn't think it through.

200
00:17:11,683 --> 00:17:13,539
I'm sorry.

201
00:17:14,099 --> 00:17:16,672
I think I was being too sensitive.

202
00:17:27,317 --> 00:17:32,023
You and Jun Kyung are living together, right?

203
00:17:32,574 --> 00:17:37,130
Which basically means
you're already a common-law couple.

204
00:17:37,130 --> 00:17:40,976
You're really just one step away.

205
00:17:41,543 --> 00:17:43,210
Just one more step.

206
00:17:43,210 --> 00:17:46,030
This is hard for her right now.

207
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:50,143
Right.

208
00:17:50,679 --> 00:17:52,440
I mean...

209
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,760
My job's unstable,

210
00:17:55,633 --> 00:17:57,860
- and I have a kid.
- Right?

211
00:17:57,860 --> 00:18:02,825
If there's even one percent doubt
behind a proposal,

212
00:18:02,825 --> 00:18:04,645
it never feels right.

213
00:18:05,632 --> 00:18:07,665
This isn't about her.

214
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:11,926
It's not because of the kid?

215
00:18:11,926 --> 00:18:14,279
And it's not because of the kid's mom?

216
00:18:15,133 --> 00:18:17,000
Then what is it?

217
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,160
This isn't your issue.

218
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:21,124
For Jun Kyung,

219
00:18:21,124 --> 00:18:23,799
marriage itself... you know,

220
00:18:23,799 --> 00:18:24,940
how do I put this...

221
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:28,420
she's already run it through her head
a thousand times,

222
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:31,940
every useless scenario included.

223
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:35,700
That's what smart, pessimistic people do.

224
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,204
The point is,

225
00:18:37,204 --> 00:18:40,904
it's not about you or anyone else.

226
00:18:42,763 --> 00:18:44,867
Jun Kyung has this thing...

227
00:18:44,867 --> 00:18:48,546
an obsession that she can never fail.

228
00:18:48,546 --> 00:18:50,940
Like... perfectionism, basically.

229
00:18:51,519 --> 00:18:53,320
It's because of me.

230
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:58,174
Hard to understand, right?

231
00:19:00,696 --> 00:19:02,167
Yeah.

232
00:19:02,690 --> 00:19:05,154
I really don't get it,

233
00:19:05,154 --> 00:19:07,454
and I can't relate at all.

234
00:19:09,610 --> 00:19:12,050
Do Hyun is a genuinely good guy.

235
00:19:12,936 --> 00:19:15,100
He showed me that happiness

236
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:18,966
comes from being with someone.

237
00:19:20,336 --> 00:19:22,356
So what's the problem?

238
00:19:24,257 --> 00:19:26,276
I'm not confident.

239
00:19:31,310 --> 00:19:34,347
Just dealing with
what I already know is overwhelming.

240
00:19:34,347 --> 00:19:37,279
If something unexpected happens between us,

241
00:19:37,279 --> 00:19:40,450
some kind of disaster we can't control...

242
00:19:42,536 --> 00:19:46,222
I know I'd want to run away.

243
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:52,959
Yeah.

244
00:19:52,959 --> 00:19:56,465
Your dad must've had it hard, right?

245
00:19:57,466 --> 00:19:59,340
No.

246
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:01,913
I think my mom had it harder.

247
00:20:03,746 --> 00:20:07,052
Not able to hold on, not able to let go.

248
00:20:08,459 --> 00:20:11,452
I think she suffered more.

249
00:20:38,745 --> 00:20:39,919
How bad is it?

250
00:20:39,919 --> 00:20:41,812
Total meltdown.

251
00:20:42,290 --> 00:20:43,783
What about Jun Kyung?

252
00:20:43,783 --> 00:20:45,070
She's sincere.

253
00:20:45,070 --> 00:20:47,323
Enough to give up a diamond.

254
00:20:48,143 --> 00:20:51,070
I've never seen Do Hyun this serious.

255
00:20:51,070 --> 00:20:52,910
You don't think...

256
00:20:52,910 --> 00:20:55,143
they're breaking up, right?

257
00:20:55,889 --> 00:20:58,294
A couple who dated long enough,
at the right age,

258
00:20:58,294 --> 00:21:00,760
but can't move to the next step?

259
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:02,105
Yeah, it happens.

260
00:21:02,105 --> 00:21:04,610
Even when they're clearly in love?

261
00:21:04,610 --> 00:21:07,285
Love is supposed to end in marriage.

262
00:21:07,285 --> 00:21:09,810
That's how social animals are wired.

263
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:11,790
Love and marriage go together.

264
00:21:11,790 --> 00:21:13,110
That's legit.

265
00:21:13,110 --> 00:21:15,434
If someone isn't right to stay with,

266
00:21:15,434 --> 00:21:18,574
instinct pushes you to find someone who is.

267
00:21:19,830 --> 00:21:21,776
Are you really hurt by this?

268
00:21:23,776 --> 00:21:25,483
No.

269
00:21:29,539 --> 00:21:31,011
Maybe a little.

270
00:21:31,733 --> 00:21:33,272
Just a little hurt.

271
00:21:35,719 --> 00:21:37,412
I'm sorry.

272
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,400
I believe

273
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:57,926
your right moment will come.

274
00:22:03,062 --> 00:22:04,999
I'll wait for it,

275
00:22:04,999 --> 00:22:07,065
with an open heart.

276
00:22:26,516 --> 00:22:27,970
Thank you

277
00:22:27,970 --> 00:22:29,762
for understanding.

278
00:22:43,906 --> 00:22:46,652
This thing's completely rotten.

279
00:22:52,866 --> 00:22:55,232
Whoa, you scared me.

280
00:22:59,060 --> 00:23:00,980
Can you even do this?

281
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:03,373
You've never done it before.

282
00:23:03,373 --> 00:23:04,940
Shouldn't we call someone?

283
00:23:04,940 --> 00:23:07,100
It's our house.
We can't call people every time.

284
00:23:07,100 --> 00:23:09,126
I'll handle it.

285
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:12,359
- Want some help?
- No, it's fine.

286
00:23:12,359 --> 00:23:13,744
It's dangerous. Get down.

287
00:23:13,744 --> 00:23:15,127
Get down.

288
00:23:15,127 --> 00:23:16,883
It's dangerous.

289
00:23:18,995 --> 00:23:21,406
Are you still mad?

290
00:23:21,406 --> 00:23:23,680
Who says I'm mad?

291
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:25,373
Just get down.

292
00:23:27,926 --> 00:23:29,386
Okay.

293
00:23:32,810 --> 00:23:34,875
What do you take me for?

294
00:23:34,875 --> 00:23:37,253
I'll fix this perfectly.

295
00:23:37,253 --> 00:23:39,199
This is nothing.

296
00:23:41,753 --> 00:23:43,599
That's loud.

297
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,712
This is easy.

298
00:23:49,045 --> 00:23:50,900
Geez, that hurts.

299
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:52,031
- Are you okay?
- Wait, hold on.

300
00:23:52,031 --> 00:23:54,231
Ja Yeong, help me! I've been shot.

301
00:23:54,231 --> 00:23:55,846
It hurts.

302
00:23:56,773 --> 00:23:59,060
- Gosh!
- Oh no, what do we do?

303
00:23:59,060 --> 00:24:00,918
No, don't come up.

304
00:24:00,918 --> 00:24:03,224
Get down. I'll handle it.

305
00:24:03,224 --> 00:24:05,250
Don't pull it!

306
00:24:10,709 --> 00:24:12,575
Hey, don't touch it.

307
00:24:20,478 --> 00:24:22,476
Did you just laugh?

308
00:24:23,918 --> 00:24:25,684
Sorry.

309
00:24:26,905 --> 00:24:29,985
But the way you look right now...

310
00:24:30,735 --> 00:24:32,865
I can't handle this.

311
00:24:36,836 --> 00:24:38,979
Cheers.

312
00:24:42,775 --> 00:24:44,160
Feel lighter now?

313
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:45,880
You did great.

314
00:24:45,880 --> 00:24:48,500
I wanted to treat you to something better.

315
00:24:48,500 --> 00:24:50,681
Every time I write late at night,

316
00:24:50,681 --> 00:24:54,260
I crave a thick seafood pancake.

317
00:24:54,260 --> 00:24:57,180
I tell myself I'll get it tomorrow,
then forget.

318
00:24:57,180 --> 00:24:59,780
And every night, I think of it again.

319
00:24:59,780 --> 00:25:02,560
You look really happy.

320
00:25:02,560 --> 00:25:04,965
Sounds like good news.

321
00:25:04,965 --> 00:25:07,086
Is it that obvious?

322
00:25:07,580 --> 00:25:09,880
This is kind of a brag...

323
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:13,091
My boyfriend is not a professor though,

324
00:25:13,091 --> 00:25:15,933
but it looks like he'll be teaching
at a university soon.

325
00:25:17,146 --> 00:25:19,780
That's double good news.

326
00:25:19,780 --> 00:25:22,593
I thought you'd already heard.

327
00:25:22,593 --> 00:25:24,220
Heard what?

328
00:25:31,565 --> 00:25:32,798
So...

329
00:25:32,798 --> 00:25:34,660
I picked the materials for the sophomore class.

330
00:25:34,660 --> 00:25:36,200
I'm still organizing the junior class.

331
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:37,958
Thanks.

332
00:25:39,993 --> 00:25:41,600
I heard from Professor Choi.

333
00:25:41,600 --> 00:25:43,728
Congratulations.

334
00:25:43,728 --> 00:25:45,728
It's thanks to you.

335
00:25:46,413 --> 00:25:48,174
Thank you.

336
00:25:48,174 --> 00:25:52,647
The semester's almost over, so finish strong.

337
00:25:53,620 --> 00:25:56,476
- Okay.
- Yeah, wrap things up and head out.

338
00:25:57,920 --> 00:26:01,551
If you need anything while prepping lectures,

339
00:26:01,551 --> 00:26:04,413
or have questions, come see me anytime.

340
00:26:06,361 --> 00:26:08,400
Professor.

341
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,714
Yeah?

342
00:26:11,150 --> 00:26:12,595
Well...

343
00:26:13,140 --> 00:26:15,299
Make it quick. I have a class soon.

344
00:26:16,420 --> 00:26:17,900
No, it's nothing.

345
00:26:17,900 --> 00:26:20,354
I'll do my best till the end.

346
00:26:20,354 --> 00:26:22,493
- Great, go for it!
- Yeah.

347
00:26:34,133 --> 00:26:35,580
Hey, it's me.

348
00:26:35,580 --> 00:26:37,200
I have a quick question.

349
00:26:37,200 --> 00:26:39,040
Sure, go ahead.

350
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:42,786
These days, if you want to be an adjunct,

351
00:26:42,786 --> 00:26:47,146
do you still have to pay
the supervising professor?

352
00:26:48,412 --> 00:26:50,640
What? That doesn't happen anymore.

353
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:52,646
Why?

354
00:26:52,646 --> 00:26:54,440
It wasn't Professor Song, was it?

355
00:26:54,440 --> 00:26:56,840
No. Someone just asked me.

356
00:26:56,840 --> 00:26:58,160
Thanks.

357
00:26:58,160 --> 00:27:00,113
I'll call you later.

358
00:27:00,113 --> 00:27:01,553
Okay.

359
00:27:16,536 --> 00:27:17,895
Hey.

360
00:27:17,895 --> 00:27:19,931
Jun Seo.

361
00:27:20,585 --> 00:27:21,930
- Get up. Come on.
- Why?

362
00:27:21,930 --> 00:27:23,094
Get up. Take my hand.

363
00:27:23,094 --> 00:27:24,436
Why?

364
00:27:30,866 --> 00:27:32,217
What is it?

365
00:27:32,217 --> 00:27:34,810
Our big-mouthed writer says...

366
00:27:34,810 --> 00:27:36,523
- Yeah?
- I...

367
00:27:38,404 --> 00:27:40,299
I won the grand prize.

368
00:27:40,299 --> 00:27:41,705
Oh, really?

369
00:27:43,983 --> 00:27:47,647
At our publishing house contest...

370
00:27:47,647 --> 00:27:50,080
I won first place.

371
00:27:51,509 --> 00:27:53,436
- I can't believe this.
- You earned it.

372
00:27:53,436 --> 00:27:55,882
- Well done.
- I'm so happy.

373
00:27:59,083 --> 00:28:01,330
Did you pack your toothbrush and towel?

374
00:28:01,330 --> 00:28:03,510
Yeah, I packed everything.

375
00:28:05,230 --> 00:28:08,438
You said you wanted to go camping.
Perfect timing.

376
00:28:08,438 --> 00:28:09,570
Yeah.

377
00:28:09,570 --> 00:28:13,370
Jun Seo and Hye On are hilarious.

378
00:28:17,873 --> 00:28:20,272
What are you gonna do, Mom?

379
00:28:20,851 --> 00:28:23,098
You'll be home alone.

380
00:28:23,098 --> 00:28:25,347
I've got plenty to do.

381
00:28:25,347 --> 00:28:27,450
I'll meet friends and have fun.

382
00:28:27,450 --> 00:28:29,347
Mom.

383
00:28:29,347 --> 00:28:30,647
Even so...

384
00:28:31,453 --> 00:28:33,426
don't forget

385
00:28:34,186 --> 00:28:35,506
to feed Oscar.

386
00:28:35,506 --> 00:28:38,173
You think I'd forget to feed Oscar?

387
00:28:38,753 --> 00:28:40,490
No, I mean...

388
00:28:40,490 --> 00:28:41,918
actually, once before,

389
00:28:41,918 --> 00:28:44,171
I skipped his food on purpose.

390
00:28:46,457 --> 00:28:48,184
Because I didn't like

391
00:28:49,391 --> 00:28:51,031
Jun Kyung.

392
00:28:54,856 --> 00:28:56,656
I think Dad's here.

393
00:28:57,396 --> 00:28:59,749
- I'm heading out.
- Have fun.

394
00:29:05,948 --> 00:29:07,946
You're washing my face,

395
00:29:07,946 --> 00:29:09,605
and washing my hair...

396
00:29:09,605 --> 00:29:12,065
I'm really being spoiled.

397
00:29:12,585 --> 00:29:15,395
Getting hurt has its perks.

398
00:29:15,395 --> 00:29:18,180
Maybe I should injure my right hand next time.

399
00:29:18,180 --> 00:29:20,426
Then you'd feed me too, right?

400
00:29:20,426 --> 00:29:22,625
Can you stop talking?

401
00:29:22,625 --> 00:29:24,991
They'll be here any minute.

402
00:29:26,072 --> 00:29:27,865
Okay, rinsing now.

403
00:29:27,865 --> 00:29:29,718
Feels good, right?

404
00:29:36,846 --> 00:29:39,380
- Dad!
- Thanks for coming all this way.

405
00:29:42,086 --> 00:29:44,140
- Hello.
- Hi.

406
00:29:45,306 --> 00:29:47,172
Wow, you've grown so much.

407
00:29:52,066 --> 00:29:53,779
Get it, get it.

408
00:29:55,353 --> 00:29:56,960
Did you get one?

409
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:58,239
Jun Kyung!

410
00:29:58,239 --> 00:29:59,699
Look at this.

411
00:30:01,104 --> 00:30:03,551
There are so many fish, but he can't catch any.

412
00:30:03,551 --> 00:30:05,932
How can you miss with this many?

413
00:30:05,932 --> 00:30:08,052
Seriously, why can't you catch one?

414
00:30:17,544 --> 00:30:19,417
The more I see Do Hyun,

415
00:30:20,664 --> 00:30:24,023
the more I think... he's a really good guy.

416
00:30:26,424 --> 00:30:28,563
You think so too?

417
00:30:29,211 --> 00:30:30,670
Yeah.

418
00:30:30,670 --> 00:30:33,483
You two look really great together.

419
00:30:40,276 --> 00:30:42,122
Then why are you hesitating?

420
00:30:45,562 --> 00:30:46,871
Jun Kyung.

421
00:30:48,984 --> 00:30:52,283
It wasn't all hardship for me.

422
00:30:54,772 --> 00:30:58,239
You might not know it yet.

423
00:30:58,239 --> 00:31:00,132
That's why...

424
00:31:00,132 --> 00:31:01,911
you're scared.

425
00:31:03,005 --> 00:31:05,344
But someday, you'll understand.

426
00:31:06,672 --> 00:31:09,919
Love isn't just about being happy

427
00:31:09,919 --> 00:31:12,445
and having fun together.

428
00:31:19,035 --> 00:31:21,615
Sometimes it's feeling tender,

429
00:31:24,653 --> 00:31:26,599
feeling worried...

430
00:31:27,987 --> 00:31:30,593
that's love too.

431
00:31:34,877 --> 00:31:37,223
I was happy.

432
00:31:39,175 --> 00:31:41,241
And I was grateful for all of it.

433
00:31:50,123 --> 00:31:52,203
I'm sorry you saw the part of me

434
00:31:54,510 --> 00:31:56,649
that wanted to let go,

435
00:31:59,415 --> 00:32:01,961
that wanted to run away.

436
00:32:08,799 --> 00:32:10,099
Jun Kyung.

437
00:32:10,896 --> 00:32:12,796
Don't be afraid.

438
00:32:14,310 --> 00:32:16,363
You're much stronger

439
00:32:16,363 --> 00:32:18,896
than I ever was.

440
00:32:32,100 --> 00:32:33,959
Whoa, I got one!

441
00:32:35,461 --> 00:32:37,555
Got it! Nice!

442
00:32:37,555 --> 00:32:39,148
Jun Kyung!

443
00:32:39,994 --> 00:32:42,287
- Look at this.
- We caught a ton!

444
00:33:14,189 --> 00:33:15,489
Okay.

445
00:33:16,596 --> 00:33:19,602
Let's find the hope that anxiety tried to hide.

446
00:33:21,083 --> 00:33:23,909
Even if I don't turn out the way I imagine,

447
00:33:24,696 --> 00:33:26,989
I won't be disappointed.

448
00:33:28,569 --> 00:33:30,822
I chose to trust myself.

449
00:33:32,809 --> 00:33:35,142
And the moment I decided that,

450
00:33:36,330 --> 00:33:38,424
I realized it.

451
00:33:41,816 --> 00:33:43,395
What was I...

452
00:33:44,597 --> 00:33:46,536
so afraid of?

453
00:33:52,217 --> 00:33:54,628
- You ate two peppers?
- Careful, it's hot.

454
00:33:54,628 --> 00:33:56,050
You ate it?

455
00:33:56,050 --> 00:33:58,649
Oh, my goodness.

456
00:34:01,523 --> 00:34:03,909
I have something to say.

457
00:34:07,429 --> 00:34:09,477
I'm going to get married...

458
00:34:09,477 --> 00:34:11,076
to Do Hyun.

459
00:34:38,336 --> 00:34:40,246
If you were going to say yes anyway,

460
00:34:40,246 --> 00:34:42,412
why not from the beginning?

461
00:34:43,596 --> 00:34:45,316
You know

462
00:34:45,316 --> 00:34:47,253
how hard that was for me.

463
00:34:47,253 --> 00:34:50,653
Back then... those feelings were real.

464
00:34:55,131 --> 00:34:57,578
So what happened...

465
00:34:59,028 --> 00:35:01,608
to those feelings?

466
00:35:05,016 --> 00:35:06,689
Well... greed?

467
00:35:06,689 --> 00:35:10,993
That diamond ring kept catching my eye.

468
00:35:22,168 --> 00:35:23,779
No matter how much I think about it,

469
00:35:23,779 --> 00:35:26,445
there's not a single reason

470
00:35:26,445 --> 00:35:28,705
not to marry you.

471
00:35:39,648 --> 00:35:41,328
Ju Do Hyun.

472
00:35:43,948 --> 00:35:46,248
Will you marry me?

473
00:35:54,158 --> 00:35:55,565
Wait.

474
00:35:57,838 --> 00:36:00,824
Are you proposing to me right now?

475
00:36:02,639 --> 00:36:04,092
Yeah.

476
00:36:09,892 --> 00:36:11,192
Yes.

477
00:36:13,193 --> 00:36:15,026
I want to marry you,

478
00:36:17,306 --> 00:36:18,792
Jun Kyung.

479
00:36:29,312 --> 00:36:31,472
(In German) I miss those days.

480
00:36:31,986 --> 00:36:35,512
After a performance, you'd walk me out.

481
00:36:36,392 --> 00:36:38,698
That's a manager's job.

482
00:36:39,499 --> 00:36:40,716
So, how is it?

483
00:36:40,716 --> 00:36:44,159
You had a reason for going to Korea.
How's that going?

484
00:36:44,159 --> 00:36:46,459
It's not easy.

485
00:36:46,459 --> 00:36:47,876
Why?

486
00:36:47,876 --> 00:36:50,029
Wasn't it something you wanted badly?

487
00:36:50,029 --> 00:36:52,329
Maybe someone else wants it more.

488
00:36:53,432 --> 00:36:54,789
Yun Ju.

489
00:36:54,789 --> 00:36:57,655
You said you couldn't breathe here.

490
00:36:58,566 --> 00:37:00,866
You left to survive.

491
00:37:02,279 --> 00:37:03,623
What are you doing?

492
00:37:03,623 --> 00:37:06,009
It's your birthday, and you're drinking alone?

493
00:37:08,752 --> 00:37:10,932
I miss you, Anna.

494
00:37:11,539 --> 00:37:13,809
You can come back anytime.

495
00:37:13,809 --> 00:37:17,422
You have family here too.

496
00:37:18,087 --> 00:37:19,480
Me.

497
00:37:20,514 --> 00:37:22,500
Thanks, Anna.

498
00:37:37,266 --> 00:37:38,566
Daniel.

499
00:37:42,306 --> 00:37:43,919
How was it?

500
00:37:46,906 --> 00:37:48,373
It was fun.

501
00:37:48,873 --> 00:37:50,173
No,

502
00:37:51,193 --> 00:37:52,946
not that.

503
00:37:55,026 --> 00:37:56,419
About me...

504
00:37:57,733 --> 00:37:59,753
marrying...

505
00:38:00,266 --> 00:38:01,899
Jun Kyung.

506
00:38:10,706 --> 00:38:12,292
Well...

507
00:38:13,273 --> 00:38:15,333
I think I'm okay with it.

508
00:38:23,086 --> 00:38:25,386
Mom will be okay too.

509
00:38:38,818 --> 00:38:40,551
Should we...

510
00:38:45,142 --> 00:38:47,955
keep it from her for now?

511
00:38:51,529 --> 00:38:52,829
Yeah.

512
00:38:54,049 --> 00:38:55,482
Good.

513
00:38:56,782 --> 00:38:58,335
About that...

514
00:38:59,642 --> 00:39:01,535
I'll tell her myself.

515
00:39:12,295 --> 00:39:14,239
Congratulations,

516
00:39:14,239 --> 00:39:15,588
Dad.

517
00:39:17,789 --> 00:39:20,388
Sorry I didn't say it earlier.

518
00:39:31,051 --> 00:39:33,611
Thank you for taking care of Jun Seo.

519
00:39:37,332 --> 00:39:39,179
Are you okay?

520
00:39:39,179 --> 00:39:42,416
I mean, you could just sleep in the bed.

521
00:39:42,416 --> 00:39:45,423
I love it. I'll sleep here.

522
00:39:45,423 --> 00:39:49,516
Okay, then I'm sleeping with you guys.

523
00:39:50,203 --> 00:39:54,836
It feels like a trip with my best friends.

524
00:39:54,836 --> 00:39:56,287
Yeah.

525
00:39:56,287 --> 00:39:58,207
Tonight feels like one of those nights

526
00:39:58,207 --> 00:40:01,170
we'll remember for a long time.

527
00:40:01,170 --> 00:40:03,789
I hate to see it end like this.

528
00:40:04,490 --> 00:40:06,048
Then...

529
00:40:06,048 --> 00:40:08,460
let's not end it.

530
00:40:08,460 --> 00:40:09,853
Yeah?

531
00:40:11,393 --> 00:40:14,320
Then... how about

532
00:40:14,320 --> 00:40:16,125
one more beer each?

533
00:40:16,125 --> 00:40:18,318
- I'm in.
- I'm in.

534
00:40:18,318 --> 00:40:20,384
Alright, I'll grab them.

535
00:40:38,267 --> 00:40:40,047
Dad, you still up?

536
00:40:41,854 --> 00:40:43,784
Can't sleep.

537
00:40:43,784 --> 00:40:45,247
You?

538
00:40:45,727 --> 00:40:47,387
Me neither.

539
00:40:53,717 --> 00:40:55,260
Why are you up?

540
00:40:55,260 --> 00:40:57,914
Looks like we're not sleeping anytime soon.

541
00:40:57,914 --> 00:40:59,947
We got caught up talking.

542
00:41:03,908 --> 00:41:05,765
Weren't you taking those with you?

543
00:41:05,765 --> 00:41:07,554
There's more.

544
00:41:12,261 --> 00:41:14,827
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

545
00:41:20,007 --> 00:41:21,828
Congratulations.

546
00:41:21,828 --> 00:41:24,005
I heard you're teaching next semester.

547
00:41:24,005 --> 00:41:26,181
Hye On wouldn't stop bragging.

548
00:41:27,188 --> 00:41:28,488
Oh...

549
00:41:30,038 --> 00:41:31,571
thanks.

550
00:41:33,985 --> 00:41:36,285
You seem more grown-up.

551
00:41:37,651 --> 00:41:40,076
I thought you'd tease Do Hyun,

552
00:41:40,076 --> 00:41:42,192
say you'd regret marrying her or something.

553
00:41:42,192 --> 00:41:44,238
Am I a kid or what?

554
00:41:47,162 --> 00:41:48,841
I used to...

555
00:41:49,415 --> 00:41:51,721
worry about things like this.

556
00:41:53,601 --> 00:41:55,232
Jun Kyung was

557
00:41:55,232 --> 00:41:57,981
beautiful, smart, and had everything,

558
00:41:59,269 --> 00:42:02,392
but I worried she hadn't met
the right person yet.

559
00:42:02,392 --> 00:42:04,129
And as for Jun Seo,

560
00:42:04,129 --> 00:42:06,791
he was handsome and kind,

561
00:42:07,935 --> 00:42:11,255
but I worried he hadn't found
what he really loved doing.

562
00:42:13,339 --> 00:42:14,782
Turns out,

563
00:42:14,782 --> 00:42:17,511
all of it was pointless worry.

564
00:42:18,325 --> 00:42:20,429
Congratulations, my daughter.

565
00:42:20,429 --> 00:42:21,489
Thank you.

566
00:42:21,489 --> 00:42:24,392
Jun Seo, just keep giving it your all.

567
00:42:24,392 --> 00:42:25,931
Okay.

568
00:42:30,812 --> 00:42:33,472
I'm truly thankful to you both.

569
00:42:35,212 --> 00:42:37,512
I didn't really do much for you.

570
00:42:42,745 --> 00:42:44,571
On a night like this...

571
00:42:45,424 --> 00:42:48,705
I wish your mom were here with us.

572
00:43:01,187 --> 00:43:03,024
Please verify your account and balance,

573
00:43:03,024 --> 00:43:05,049
then select a transaction.

574
00:43:05,049 --> 00:43:06,879
[Balance: 260,000 won]

575
00:43:14,821 --> 00:43:16,892
Please take your card.

576
00:43:16,892 --> 00:43:17,935
[24-Hour ATM]

577
00:43:17,935 --> 00:43:20,721
Please make sure you have all your belongings.

578
00:43:21,189 --> 00:43:23,650
Thank you for using our service.

579
00:43:26,968 --> 00:43:30,134
[Cash Advance Withdrawal]

580
00:43:50,758 --> 00:43:53,360
[Withdrawal Amount: 5,000,000 won]

581
00:44:05,416 --> 00:44:09,139
[Department of Media Studies,
Professor Choi Sung Min]

582
00:44:32,310 --> 00:44:35,110
We used to come here a lot
when Jun Seo was little.

583
00:44:35,110 --> 00:44:36,447
The soup here is amazing.

584
00:44:36,447 --> 00:44:37,616
Oh, really?

585
00:44:37,616 --> 00:44:39,442
Let's sit here.

586
00:44:41,556 --> 00:44:43,153
Jun Kyung?

587
00:44:43,153 --> 00:44:45,372
Chang Sik? Long time no see.

588
00:44:45,372 --> 00:44:47,172
- How've you been?
- Yeah...

589
00:44:49,823 --> 00:44:51,300
Who's this?

590
00:44:51,300 --> 00:44:52,849
Oh...

591
00:44:52,849 --> 00:44:54,850
my boyfriend.

592
00:44:54,850 --> 00:44:56,716
The one I'm marrying.

593
00:44:58,783 --> 00:45:00,329
Hello.

594
00:45:06,657 --> 00:45:09,303
Did Jun Kyung ever mention me?

595
00:45:12,537 --> 00:45:16,010
She said she had a classmate
who became a priest.

596
00:45:17,768 --> 00:45:20,394
Just... "a classmate?"

597
00:45:22,381 --> 00:45:23,860
Yeah.

598
00:45:25,695 --> 00:45:27,821
I guess...

599
00:45:27,821 --> 00:45:29,155
she really loves you, Do Jun.

600
00:45:29,155 --> 00:45:31,861
I'm Do Hyun. Ju Do Hyun.

601
00:45:31,861 --> 00:45:34,048
Oh, sorry.

602
00:45:34,048 --> 00:45:36,165
Looks like she really loves you,

603
00:45:36,165 --> 00:45:37,701
Do Hyun.

604
00:45:38,328 --> 00:45:41,301
She only called me an old classmate.

605
00:45:47,938 --> 00:45:49,424
Right.

606
00:45:50,098 --> 00:45:52,831
You probably don't need to know everything.

607
00:45:55,624 --> 00:45:57,844
Yeah, that's better.

608
00:45:58,511 --> 00:46:00,771
Better not to know too much.

609
00:46:02,257 --> 00:46:04,370
- Here you go.
- Oh, thank you.

610
00:46:04,370 --> 00:46:05,918
Thanks.

611
00:46:05,918 --> 00:46:08,101
I'm not letting you have
another priest officiate.

612
00:46:08,101 --> 00:46:09,616
What are you talking about?

613
00:46:09,616 --> 00:46:11,334
Your wedding is at our church. No exceptions.

614
00:46:11,334 --> 00:46:12,835
That's great for me.

615
00:46:12,835 --> 00:46:15,415
You know, it's hard to book venues these days.

616
00:46:15,974 --> 00:46:18,584
- Hey.
- Oh, Won Young?

617
00:46:18,584 --> 00:46:20,477
I just moved to this neighborhood.

618
00:46:20,477 --> 00:46:22,377
Really? That's great.

619
00:46:24,321 --> 00:46:26,992
This is the priest from the local church.

620
00:46:26,992 --> 00:46:28,691
He is just my old classmate.

621
00:46:28,691 --> 00:46:30,439
And this is my boyfriend.

622
00:46:31,044 --> 00:46:32,567
Nice to meet you.

623
00:46:32,567 --> 00:46:34,517
Nice to meet you.

624
00:46:35,276 --> 00:46:36,576
But...

625
00:46:37,501 --> 00:46:40,027
You look really familiar.

626
00:46:40,862 --> 00:46:42,162
Yeah...

627
00:46:42,787 --> 00:46:45,265
I feel like I've seen you before too.

628
00:46:45,265 --> 00:46:47,913
- At a convenience store...
- Do you have a criminal record?

629
00:47:22,392 --> 00:47:23,831
I don't even know

630
00:47:23,831 --> 00:47:26,477
if that pork cutlet went
in my mouth or my nose.

631
00:47:29,977 --> 00:47:32,616
If I mess up even a little around here,

632
00:47:32,616 --> 00:47:34,560
I'm in serious trouble.

633
00:47:34,560 --> 00:47:36,793
You're just realizing that now?

634
00:47:40,817 --> 00:47:43,390
I don't know if I should be
getting married like this.

635
00:47:44,491 --> 00:47:46,397
Then call it off.

636
00:47:50,344 --> 00:47:52,008
Hey, I can't do that.

637
00:47:52,008 --> 00:47:54,950
Our future's right there.

638
00:47:54,950 --> 00:47:56,591
You're funny.

639
00:47:58,118 --> 00:48:00,775
So... for our second,

640
00:48:00,775 --> 00:48:03,634
you want a boy or a girl?

641
00:48:03,634 --> 00:48:05,381
What is this, out of nowhere?

642
00:48:05,381 --> 00:48:06,921
I'd say... second, a girl.

643
00:48:06,921 --> 00:48:08,320
Then a boy.

644
00:48:10,328 --> 00:48:11,971
Who decided there's a "then?"

645
00:48:11,971 --> 00:48:14,237
So we're agreed at least on one thing.

646
00:48:14,237 --> 00:48:16,511
Second is a girl.

647
00:48:17,471 --> 00:48:18,897
Who agreed?

648
00:48:19,458 --> 00:48:21,551
Me? No, no.

649
00:48:23,645 --> 00:48:25,461
Jin Ho,

650
00:48:25,461 --> 00:48:27,485
are you almost done?

651
00:48:27,485 --> 00:48:28,831
Just a second.

652
00:48:28,831 --> 00:48:30,708
Almost done.

653
00:48:30,708 --> 00:48:32,168
Ugh, this feels so awkward.

654
00:48:32,168 --> 00:48:35,000
Come out already. I'll tell you how you look.

655
00:48:36,421 --> 00:48:37,954
It's weird, right?

656
00:48:41,228 --> 00:48:43,054
Yeah, it's weird.

657
00:48:44,253 --> 00:48:45,654
Ugh.

658
00:48:48,741 --> 00:48:50,654
Is something wrong?

659
00:48:51,201 --> 00:48:53,361
Come on, hurry. I feel so awkward.

660
00:48:55,201 --> 00:48:57,467
I feel so awkward. Hurry.

661
00:48:58,861 --> 00:49:00,860
Okay, wait.

662
00:49:01,732 --> 00:49:03,513
I'm coming.

663
00:49:52,321 --> 00:49:53,838
Simple happiness

664
00:49:53,838 --> 00:49:56,138
sometimes fills us up

665
00:49:58,481 --> 00:50:01,054
before we even notice.

666
00:50:02,820 --> 00:50:03,948
Ta-da.

667
00:50:03,948 --> 00:50:07,894
Just living our ordinary lives,
each in our own place,

668
00:50:07,894 --> 00:50:09,994
was enough...

669
00:50:12,101 --> 00:50:14,281
to feel complete.

670
00:50:21,887 --> 00:50:24,434
I wasn't expecting,

671
00:50:25,701 --> 00:50:28,247
or even hoping for, anything more.

672
00:50:30,094 --> 00:50:31,854
But life...

673
00:50:32,400 --> 00:50:34,714
has a way of placing

674
00:50:35,974 --> 00:50:38,754
the most unexpected moments
right in front of us.

675
00:50:41,628 --> 00:50:44,520
My period's late, so I thought maybe...

676
00:50:50,568 --> 00:50:52,487
Are you disappointed?

677
00:50:53,414 --> 00:50:55,827
I guess I was hoping a little.

678
00:50:57,328 --> 00:50:59,814
But now that it's actually like this,

679
00:51:01,008 --> 00:51:04,020
I'm more worried than disappointed.

680
00:51:06,788 --> 00:51:08,798
There's no rush.

681
00:51:08,798 --> 00:51:12,541
We haven't even had the wedding yet.

682
00:51:12,541 --> 00:51:14,354
Honestly,

683
00:51:15,034 --> 00:51:17,104
I haven't exactly been trying that hard.

684
00:51:17,104 --> 00:51:18,764
If I really put in the effort...

685
00:51:18,764 --> 00:51:20,614
But what if...

686
00:51:21,448 --> 00:51:22,851
what if

687
00:51:22,851 --> 00:51:24,284
something's wrong with me?

688
00:51:24,284 --> 00:51:26,844
What could possibly be wrong with you?

689
00:51:35,156 --> 00:51:37,456
I'm an OB-GYN.

690
00:51:38,949 --> 00:51:41,369
I'm 38,

691
00:51:41,369 --> 00:51:43,609
and it'd be my first pregnancy.

692
00:51:46,842 --> 00:51:48,546
Should we...

693
00:51:48,546 --> 00:51:51,062
get checked, just in case?

694
00:51:51,062 --> 00:51:52,908
At our hospital? That'd be awkward.

695
00:51:52,908 --> 00:51:55,486
Then we'll go somewhere else.

696
00:51:55,486 --> 00:51:58,372
We'll go together and get checked together.

697
00:51:58,372 --> 00:52:01,085
Why you? There's nothing wrong with you.

698
00:52:02,539 --> 00:52:04,818
That's what couples do.

699
00:52:04,818 --> 00:52:07,324
They go together.

700
00:52:44,959 --> 00:52:46,757
It's a mountain road, so it gets dark fast.

701
00:52:46,757 --> 00:52:48,084
Be careful on your way.

702
00:52:48,084 --> 00:52:49,158
Okay.

703
00:52:49,158 --> 00:52:51,343
Thank you. Bye.

704
00:53:06,297 --> 00:53:07,987
The number you have dialed is not...

705
00:53:07,987 --> 00:53:12,233
What's she so wrapped up in
that she can't answer?

706
00:53:39,165 --> 00:53:40,429
Hello.

707
00:53:40,429 --> 00:53:41,932
Where are you?

708
00:53:42,492 --> 00:53:43,849
University, obviously.

709
00:53:43,849 --> 00:53:45,123
You're staying late again?

710
00:53:45,123 --> 00:53:48,044
The professor got that research grant,
remember?

711
00:53:48,044 --> 00:53:50,605
He asked me to help till the very end.

712
00:53:52,687 --> 00:53:53,911
The professor is calling for me.

713
00:53:53,911 --> 00:53:56,410
I'm going to be late tonight,
so go to bed first.

714
00:53:56,410 --> 00:53:57,983
Bye.

715
00:54:09,210 --> 00:54:12,476
Yeah, I'm at this plaza right now.

716
00:54:13,303 --> 00:54:14,581
Oh, okay.

717
00:54:14,581 --> 00:54:17,287
- Hey, hurry up.
- Just one more.

718
00:54:17,287 --> 00:54:19,587
One more drink.

719
00:54:20,457 --> 00:54:21,881
- Over there, the car.
- Got it.

720
00:54:21,881 --> 00:54:23,247
Let's go.

721
00:54:25,021 --> 00:54:28,494
The number you have dialed is not in service.

722
00:54:49,500 --> 00:54:51,107
Ja Yeong.

723
00:54:51,107 --> 00:54:52,680
Ja Yeong!

724
00:55:06,151 --> 00:55:07,182
Ja Yeong!

725
00:55:07,182 --> 00:55:09,792
Why didn't you answer your phone?
I've been looking for you.

726
00:55:09,792 --> 00:55:11,862
What are you doing out here?

727
00:55:21,368 --> 00:55:22,698
Ja Yeong.

728
00:55:22,698 --> 00:55:24,127
Hey.

729
00:55:26,094 --> 00:55:27,561
Are you okay?

730
00:55:29,741 --> 00:55:32,167
I don't know where I am.

731
00:55:37,214 --> 00:55:39,057
I suddenly can't remember

732
00:55:39,057 --> 00:55:41,357
what I was doing here...

733
00:55:42,341 --> 00:55:44,394
I got so scared.

734
00:55:45,168 --> 00:55:47,428
I just thought I had to get home.

735
00:55:48,628 --> 00:55:51,474
I had to get back to you...

736
00:55:54,314 --> 00:55:56,614
But I don't know where I am,

737
00:55:57,481 --> 00:55:59,741
or how to get home.

738
00:56:02,494 --> 00:56:04,185
It's okay.

739
00:56:04,185 --> 00:56:05,279
I'm sorry.

740
00:56:05,279 --> 00:56:07,388
I got here late.

741
00:56:07,388 --> 00:56:08,918
It's just dark, that's all.

742
00:56:08,918 --> 00:56:11,511
The path is dark, all the trees look the same.

743
00:56:11,511 --> 00:56:14,087
- Anyone would get confused.
- No...

744
00:56:14,854 --> 00:56:16,694
I said...

745
00:56:17,474 --> 00:56:19,945
I loved this forest after we moved here.

746
00:56:19,945 --> 00:56:22,229
I walked this path every single day.

747
00:56:22,229 --> 00:56:23,942
How could I...

748
00:56:27,475 --> 00:56:29,775
How could I not know?

749
00:56:42,686 --> 00:56:44,310
Your test results look good.

750
00:56:44,310 --> 00:56:46,255
Getting pregnant shouldn't be difficult.

751
00:56:46,255 --> 00:56:48,120
Really? That's a relief.

752
00:56:48,120 --> 00:56:50,480
See? I told you it'd be fine.

753
00:56:50,480 --> 00:56:51,640
But...

754
00:56:51,640 --> 00:56:54,138
about your results, Mr. Ju Do Hyun...

755
00:56:54,138 --> 00:56:55,487
Yes?

756
00:56:56,130 --> 00:56:58,154
I'm afraid your result...

757
00:56:58,154 --> 00:57:00,454
came back negative.

758
00:57:05,570 --> 00:57:07,210
Negative?

759
00:57:08,217 --> 00:57:10,876
What does that mean?

760
00:57:13,030 --> 00:57:15,436
It means infertility.

761
00:57:19,803 --> 00:57:21,060
That can't be right.

762
00:57:21,060 --> 00:57:24,846
Of course, nothing is ever 100 percent.

763
00:57:25,429 --> 00:57:26,922
We...

764
00:57:30,690 --> 00:57:32,083
I mean,

765
00:57:32,677 --> 00:57:35,257
I already have a child.

766
00:57:38,530 --> 00:57:40,116
You do?

767
00:57:41,943 --> 00:57:44,294
Your hormone levels are quite low.

768
00:57:44,294 --> 00:57:46,814
Based on your FSH levels,

769
00:57:46,814 --> 00:57:49,892
it appears to be non-obstructive azoospermia.

770
00:57:49,892 --> 00:57:54,207
Non-obstructive means it's congenital.

771
00:57:56,741 --> 00:57:58,198
Are you sure?

772
00:57:58,198 --> 00:58:02,094
As I said,
there's no such thing as 100 percent.

773
00:58:03,634 --> 00:58:07,334
A genetic test would be
the most definitive step.

774
00:58:10,368 --> 00:58:12,164
If it were me,

775
00:58:12,164 --> 00:58:14,880
I'd talk to the child's mother.

776
00:58:25,371 --> 00:58:27,204
Do Hyun.

777
00:58:29,777 --> 00:58:31,377
Do Hyun?

778
00:58:38,931 --> 00:58:41,057
I'm coming in.

779
00:58:58,739 --> 00:59:00,746
I'm sorry.

780
00:59:00,746 --> 00:59:02,606
I guess I didn't hear you.

781
00:59:18,419 --> 00:59:19,864
I'm sorry. Because of me...

782
00:59:19,864 --> 00:59:21,894
Don't say that.

783
00:59:24,779 --> 00:59:26,225
Daniel...

784
00:59:26,812 --> 00:59:28,772
is my son.

785
00:59:31,912 --> 00:59:34,865
I'm not checking anything else.

786
00:59:35,992 --> 00:59:38,072
There's no need to.

787
00:59:40,066 --> 00:59:42,972
We can just act like
none of this ever happened.

788
00:59:45,512 --> 00:59:48,158
No, nothing actually happened.

789
00:59:49,006 --> 00:59:51,306
As long as no one knows.

790
00:59:56,851 --> 00:59:58,392
Right?

791
00:59:59,892 --> 01:00:01,358
Daniel...

792
01:00:03,552 --> 01:00:05,372
is my son.

793
01:00:16,057 --> 01:00:17,357
Yes.

794
01:00:17,997 --> 01:00:19,917
Daniel is your son.

795
01:00:22,024 --> 01:00:24,663
Promise me, Jun Kyung.

796
01:00:26,244 --> 01:00:27,970
That no one...

797
01:00:30,163 --> 01:00:32,529
will ever find out about today.

798
01:00:38,437 --> 01:00:39,757
Yeah.

799
01:00:41,991 --> 01:00:44,291
It'll be okay if no one knows.

800
01:01:05,625 --> 01:01:08,746
[Piano performance - Pianist Im Yun Ju]

801
01:01:22,837 --> 01:01:24,591
Im Yun Ju.

802
01:01:24,591 --> 01:01:26,548
I was wondering what your first official move

803
01:01:26,548 --> 01:01:28,235
back in Korea would be.

804
01:01:28,235 --> 01:01:30,208
Didn't expect it to be a commercial.

805
01:01:31,802 --> 01:01:34,359
Who reached out first?

806
01:01:34,359 --> 01:01:36,288
You or Do Hyun?

807
01:01:36,288 --> 01:01:37,459
Does that really matter?

808
01:01:37,459 --> 01:01:39,795
It's not like we're strangers.

809
01:01:39,795 --> 01:01:42,046
We're not strangers to Do Hyun either,

810
01:01:42,046 --> 01:01:43,712
but he never asked us for favors like that.

811
01:01:43,712 --> 01:01:46,241
Hey. We're not the same as her.

812
01:01:49,976 --> 01:01:52,523
But still... are you okay?

813
01:01:53,090 --> 01:01:54,390
About what?

814
01:01:55,690 --> 01:01:57,576
I heard Do Hyun's getting married.

815
01:02:11,283 --> 01:02:12,559
Who said that?

816
01:02:12,559 --> 01:02:14,026
Jung Hoon.

817
01:02:14,026 --> 01:02:16,286
I talked to him a few days ago.

818
01:02:17,789 --> 01:02:19,842
You didn't know?

819
01:02:28,725 --> 01:02:30,957
So you're getting married.

820
01:02:34,544 --> 01:02:37,131
You don't seem like you're here
to congratulate me.

821
01:02:37,131 --> 01:02:38,931
What do you want?

822
01:02:39,871 --> 01:02:42,584
I'm thinking of giving it a try.

823
01:02:43,804 --> 01:02:45,623
Trying what?

824
01:02:46,811 --> 01:02:49,111
I'm moving to this neighborhood.

825
01:02:50,525 --> 01:02:51,276
What?

826
01:02:51,276 --> 01:02:52,909
I already found a place.

827
01:02:52,909 --> 01:02:55,074
I'm moving in next month.

828
01:02:55,898 --> 01:02:57,644
Honestly...

829
01:02:58,224 --> 01:03:00,425
marriage isn't that big a deal.

830
01:03:00,425 --> 01:03:05,225
You know, Do Hyun and I broke up
even with Daniel between us.

831
01:03:05,225 --> 01:03:07,785
And it hasn't even happened yet.

832
01:03:10,078 --> 01:03:11,675
What exactly are you trying to do?

833
01:03:11,675 --> 01:03:14,088
If you were me, what would you do?

834
01:03:15,225 --> 01:03:17,831
If I can't win anyway...

835
01:03:18,318 --> 01:03:20,864
wouldn't you want to tear it all down?

836
01:03:22,394 --> 01:03:24,084
You think people's feelings are a game?

837
01:03:24,084 --> 01:03:27,420
If Daniel lived closer to his dad,
he would be so happy.

838
01:03:28,258 --> 01:03:30,231
For Daniel...

839
01:03:31,025 --> 01:03:34,291
I'd make an even more selfish choice.

840
01:03:34,291 --> 01:03:36,537
You don't even know what Do Hyun thinks.

841
01:03:38,393 --> 01:03:41,897
He'd definitely be happy
if his son moved nearby.

842
01:03:56,032 --> 01:03:58,131
I had something to ask.

843
01:04:00,752 --> 01:04:03,505
Is Daniel really Do Hyun's son?

844
01:04:06,711 --> 01:04:08,031
What?

845
01:04:08,705 --> 01:04:11,998
Is Daniel actually his biological son?

846
01:04:52,592 --> 01:04:54,470
I'm only going to get more famous,

847
01:04:54,470 --> 01:04:55,864
do even better.

848
01:04:55,864 --> 01:04:57,911
If that happens, the pressure is on you.

849
01:04:57,911 --> 01:05:01,498
I have zero intention of congratulating you.

850
01:05:01,498 --> 01:05:02,576
You're doing this

851
01:05:02,576 --> 01:05:04,685
because you want to break up with me, huh?

852
01:05:04,685 --> 01:05:07,072
You idiot...

853
01:05:07,072 --> 01:05:08,409
Don't worry.

854
01:05:08,409 --> 01:05:11,712
We're just here to make sure everything's okay.

855
01:05:12,712 --> 01:05:15,902
I truly wanted you to be happy.

856
01:05:15,902 --> 01:05:18,972
I thought I'd be happy by your side too.

857
01:05:18,972 --> 01:05:21,418
But... I don't think I can.

858
01:05:24,152 --> 01:05:25,963
Do you really think that?

859
01:05:25,963 --> 01:05:28,335
That Daniel might not be your son?

860
01:05:28,335 --> 01:05:30,535
Is liking you

861
01:05:30,535 --> 01:05:33,308
something I deserve to be punished for?

862
01:05:33,308 --> 01:05:34,819
Why did you do it?

863
01:05:34,819 --> 01:05:36,459
You promised

864
01:05:36,459 --> 01:05:38,385
not to say anything.

865
01:05:38,385 --> 01:05:40,412
I know I was wrong, but...

866
01:05:40,412 --> 01:05:41,619
I just...

867
01:05:41,619 --> 01:05:44,765
I wish he would hold on to me.
